 These are the same flags as DPI Switch's `tools\build-mihomo.ps1`.
 
+## System hosts and tunnel routing
+
+DPI Switch enables `dns.system-hosts-direct-only: true`, keeps
+`dns.use-system-hosts: true`, and sets `ignore-system-hosts: true` on both
+WireGuard outbounds. These switches are additions of this fork.
+
+System hosts is deferred until the actual direct adapter. The routing stages
+retain the domain and a per-flow pin; `Pure`, sniffing, retries and fallback
+groups cannot replace that pin with an address resolved inside a tunnel.
+DIRECT and direct-split connect only to the pinned address, or fail. A missing
+or unreadable hosts file fails closed for named direct connections. Configured
+YAML hosts retain their upstream meaning. Tunnel DNS uses a per-request context
+to skip system hosts and never falls back to the OS resolver.
+
+Client DNS still answers with system hosts addresses and suppresses protected
+names' HTTPS/SVCB hints, including when fake-IP filtering skips a name. Tunnel
+answers remain internal. No code edits the system hosts file or relies on the
+supervisor staying alive. Existing local-network routing and sniff exclusions
+are unchanged. Applications independently bypassing hosts are outside this
+name-resolution guarantee.
+
+The DPI Switch prober also refuses direct diagnostic connections for protected
+names, including the unnamed TLS control and QUIC. This is required because a
+probe may otherwise send an IP literal that the core cannot associate with the
+name before connecting.
+
